    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Left hand osteoarthritis (M19.042)</content>. Clear improvement: pain 3 of 10 (from 7 at intake), PROMIS upper extremity T-score 42 (from 33), left grip 17 kg (from 14). The injection, hand therapy, splinting, and tool changes are working together. [S]<list><item>Continue exercises, splint, gel, and acetaminophen as needed.</item><item>A repeat injection only if pain returns, no sooner than three months after the last.</item><item>Thumb-base surgery is not needed at this level of pain and function.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Gout (M1A.9XX0)</content>. No flare. [S]<list><item>Serum urate in October, six months after the last.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">History of urinary stones (Z87.442)</content>. No symptoms. [S]<list><item>Continue about 2 L of water a day.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Hand pain, 0 to 10 numeric rating</td><td>Each clinical encounter; after each therapeutic trial</td><td>Completed today</td><td>3 of 10, down from 5 in April and 7 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Validated function measure (PROMIS upper extremity T-score; AUSCAN and FIHOA have no LOINC code)</td><td>Each clinical encounter</td><td>Completed today</td><td>T-score 42 (population mean 50; higher is better)</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Grip strength by dynamometer</td><td>Each clinical encounter in this plan</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Left 17 kg, right 23 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Pain and function reassessment 4 to 6 weeks after the injection</td><td>After each therapeutic trial</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not done: no review was booked, a deviation from the protocol; a nurse telephone call at five weeks recorded improvement without a score. No harm: the scores today show a good response. Corrective action: post-injection reviews are now booked at the time of the injection</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Joint examination</td><td>Each clinical encounter</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No synovitis; tenderness reduced</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Occupational hand therapy</td><td>First-line care</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Four sessions completed from mid-May to mid-June; home program continues</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Analgesic review: no oral NSAIDs; acetaminophen dose</td><td>Each clinical encounter</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No ibuprofen; acetaminophen about 1 g a day; gel twice a day</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>ALT on regular acetaminophen</td><td>Periodically</td><td>Due</td><td>Due at the October review</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise, joint protection, splint, and tool adaptation</td><td>Each clinical encounter</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily exercises; padded grips, a lighter mallet, and rest breaks every 45 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Gait, balance, and activities of daily living</td><td>Ongoing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Independent; no falls; never climbs a ladder alone</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Mood, sleep, and coping screen</td><td>Periodically</td><td>Due</td><td>No concerns raised; PHQ-2 planned at the wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Serum urate</td><td>Every 6 months at target</td><td>Up to date</td><td>5.4 mg/dL in March; due in October</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Hand pain at or below 3 of 10 on most days by the seven-month review. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>Carve for at least three hours a morning and write his own letters. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>No oral NSAID use and creatinine back to his baseline. Outcome by 2026-04-13: Ibuprofen stopped; creatinine from 1.21 to 1.02 mg/dL [S]</item><item>Serum urate below 6 mg/dL and no gout flare or stone. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>No falls, with safe ladder and scaffold use. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); 2020 American College of Rheumatology Guideline for the Management of Gout (2020); Medical Management of Kidney Stones: AUA Guideline (2014, amended 2019); American Geriatrics Society 2023 Updated AGS Beers Criteria for Potentially Inappropriate Medication Use in Older Adults (2023); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Annual wellness visit in September. Hand and gout review in October with serum urate, kidney tests, and ALT. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-14: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

